# =============================================================================
# DEM310 — Cosmos DB connection settings
#
# Quick start:
#   1. Copy this file:
#         PowerShell:  Copy-Item .env.example .env
#         bash/zsh:    cp .env.example .env
#   2. Edit `.env` only if you are NOT using the local emulator on the
#      default endpoint (for example: pointing at an Azure Cosmos DB
#      account, or using the Linux vNext preview emulator on a different
#      port).
#   3. Every script under /src reads these via python-dotenv before it
#      constructs the CosmosClient. `.env` is gitignored — never commit it.
#
# NOTE: the COSMOS_KEY value below is the well-known **public** key that
# ships with every Cosmos DB emulator. It is intentionally checked in to
# this example file. For Azure Cosmos DB accounts, replace it with a real
# key (or, better, switch to AAD/managed identity).
# =============================================================================

# Local Cosmos DB emulator (Windows classic, default port)
COSMOS_ENDPOINT=https://localhost:8081
COSMOS_KEY=C2y6yDjf5/R+ob0N8A7Cgv30VRDJIWEHLM+4QDU5DE2nQ9nDuVTqobD4b8mGGyPMbIZnqyMsEcaGQy67XIw/Jw==

# Database name. Each iteration ships its own default so all four scenarios
# can coexist in a single Cosmos DB account:
#
#   iteration-01 / naive-a  ->  Build26DEM310DB-i1a
#   iteration-01 / naive-b  ->  Build26DEM310DB-i1b
#   iteration-02            ->  Build26DEM310DB-i2
#   iteration-03            ->  Build26DEM310DB-i2  (tuning pass on iter-2)
#   iteration-04            ->  Build26DEM310DB-i4
#
# Iteration 3 deliberately reuses iteration 2's containers (CustomerOrders +
# Products) because it only adds composite indexes; it does NOT seed its
# own data. Seed iteration 2 first, then run iteration 3 against the same
# database.
#
# Uncomment + set COSMOS_DB ONLY if you want to force every iteration to
# use the same database (e.g. you're running a single iteration in isolation
# and want a tidy name). Leaving it unset is the recommended default.
# COSMOS_DB=Build26DEM310DB-i1a

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Alternative profiles — uncomment ONE block instead of the defaults above.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Linux vNext preview emulator (Docker, HTTP on 8081)
# COSMOS_ENDPOINT=http://localhost:8081
# COSMOS_KEY=C2y6yDjf5/R+ob0N8A7Cgv30VRDJIWEHLM+4QDU5DE2nQ9nDuVTqobD4b8mGGyPMbIZnqyMsEcaGQy67XIw/Jw==

# Azure Cosmos DB account
# COSMOS_ENDPOINT=https://<your-account>.documents.azure.com:443/
# COSMOS_KEY=<your-primary-or-secondary-key>

# =============================================================================
# Iteration 4 - cloud Cosmos DB + Azure AI Foundry (optional)
#
# Iteration 4 (hybrid + vector search) cannot run on the local emulator.
# After you run src/iteration-04-hybrid-vector-search/infra/deploy.ps1 the
# script prints the values for this block - paste them in below. Auth is
# Entra ID only (no keys); the iteration-4 scripts always use
# DefaultAzureCredential.
#
# Iterations 1-3 ignore every FOUNDRY_* / COSMOS_CONTAINER_I4 variable;
# leaving them defined does no harm.
# =============================================================================

# COSMOS_ENDPOINT=https://cosmos-dem310x.documents.azure.com:443/
# COSMOS_DB=Build26DEM310DB-i4
# COSMOS_CONTAINER_I4=ProductsRich

# Azure AI Foundry (Cognitive Services / AIServices) endpoint + deployments.
# FOUNDRY_ENDPOINT=https://aif-dem310x.cognitiveservices.azure.com/
# FOUNDRY_CHAT_DEPLOYMENT=gpt-4o-mini
# FOUNDRY_EMBEDDING_DEPLOYMENT=text-embedding-3-small
# FOUNDRY_EMBEDDING_DIMENSIONS=1536
# FOUNDRY_API_VERSION=2024-10-21
